{"book":19,"chapter":17,"rubric":"STORAGE / CHAPTER 17","slides":[{"title":"RAID is not a backup","sub":"Chapter 17 · Storage","short":"Why","main":"RAID survives a disk failure, not a human mistake.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Failure","md","Tools","Not a backup"],"captions":["A disk will die one day; will the server stop with it?","Kernel RAID (md) joins disks into one block device","mdadm manages the array, SMART warns about failure in advance","RAID does not protect against human error, a virus or a fire"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a disk will die: will the server stop?","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a disk will die: will the server stop?","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"md: disks → one /dev/md0","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a disk will die: will the server stop?","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"md: disks → one /dev/md0","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"mdadm manages, SMART warns","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"a disk will die: will the server stop?","tone":"muted","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"md: disks → one /dev/md0","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"mdadm manages, SMART warns","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"RAID ≠ backup","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[8.9,17.2,27.2]}]},{"title":"RAID levels","sub":"Chapter 17 · Storage","short":"Levels","main":"Each level has its own capacity and failure tolerance.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["raid0","raid1","raid5/6","raid10"],"captions":["raid0 stripes: full capacity, but any failure kills everything","raid1 mirrors: one disk of capacity, lives while one is intact","raid5 survives one failure, raid6 two; capacity is 1 or 2 disks less","md raid10 is not nested RAID: it works with an odd number of disks"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid0: N×\nfailures: 0","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid0: N×\nfailures: 0","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":265.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid1: 1×\nfailures: N−1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid0: N×\nfailures: 0","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":265.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid1: 1×\nfailures: N−1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":95.0,"y":110.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid5: (N−1)×\nraid6: (N−2)×","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":95.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid0: N×\nfailures: 0","tone":"red","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":265.0,"y":50.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid1: 1×\nfailures: N−1","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":95.0,"y":110.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid5: (N−1)×\nraid6: (N−2)×","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":265.0,"y":110.0,"w":158.0,"h":46.0,"text":"raid10: N/2×\nodd N is fine","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[9.1,18.3,28.3]}]},{"title":"The price of writes and rebuilds","sub":"Chapter 17 · Storage","short":"Price","main":"A small write is costly, and a rebuild reads every disk fully.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["raid5","raid6","Rebuild","Check"],"captions":["raid5: read old data and parity, write new: 4 operations","raid6: two parities, 6 operations; the driver picks the cheaper way","A rebuild reads all surviving disks: on big disks the read-error risk grows","For big disks raid6 or raid10 and a regular check of the array"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"raid5: 2 reads + 2 writes","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"raid5: 2 reads + 2 writes","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"raid6: 3 reads + 3 writes","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"raid5: 2 reads + 2 writes","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"raid6: 3 reads + 3 writes","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"rebuild: read every disk fully","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}],[{"t":"cell","id":"n0","x":180.0,"y":26.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"raid5: 2 reads + 2 writes","tone":"blue","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n1","x":180.0,"y":58.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"raid6: 3 reads + 3 writes","tone":"violet","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n2","x":180.0,"y":90.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"rebuild: read every disk fully","tone":"yellow","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"n3","x":180.0,"y":122.0,"w":280.0,"h":24.0,"text":"monthly: check","tone":"green","size":9.0,"sub_size":8.5}]],"cues":[8.0,17.5,28.1]}]},{"title":"Creating an array","sub":"Chapter 17 · Storage","short":"Create","main":"One command: level, disk count, partitions; a spare with -x.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Level","Disks","Bitmap","Background"],"caption